      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "considering so many people have \"partners\" and groups, it would be nice if indeed people could share a world. Say person 1 gets on vrchat, it loads their shared home as their home instance, and person 2 (their partner both ingame and out) logs in.. and there's no request. They are already in the world with person 1. They can talk, decide where they're gonna go, drop a portal. there's no \"joining up\" they are already joined-up by their choice to share a home.\n\nFor the case of a group, there would be \"set this world as group root\" or something like that, and then anyone can do \"use group home\" and similarly to the partner one multiple people log in, and get sent to the same \"group home\" instance, which is of course unloaded when the last member leaves, and a new one is made when the first member goes home. It's just a basic idea of \"does this user have group home set? yes, check group. is there a home instance live? Yes. Okay, go there.  No? make one, go there.\" which then lets all other users hit the same logic gate when they \"go home\", they get \"does this user have group home set? yes, check group. is there a home instance live? Yes. Okay, go there. \"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
